    "type": "code",
    "prompt": "Your task is to write a function, listSetDifference, that takes two lists, l1 and l2, that represent sets and returns a new list representing the set difference l1 - l2. The values in the returned list may be in any order. Since the given lists represent sets, you may assume that no value appears more than once in a list.\n\nAssumptions and Constraints\n\n\tNo value appears more than once in a list.\n\tYou must not use arrays.\n\tYou must not modify the given lists.\n\n\nExamples\n\n./testListSetDifference\nEnter list 1: 4 3 1 7 6\nEnter list 2: 6 2 1 5 3\n\nSet 1: {4, 3, 1, 7, 6}\nSet 2: {6, 2, 1, 5, 3}\nDifference: {4, 7}\n\n\n./testListSetDifference\nEnter list 1: 1 3 5 7 9\nEnter list 2: 8 6 4 2 0\n\nSet 1: {1, 3, 5, 7, 9}\nSet 2: {8, 6, 4, 2, 0}\nDifference: {1, 3, 5, 7, 9}\n\n\n./testListSetDifference\nEnter list 1: 9 1 8 2 5\nEnter list 2: 1 5 2 9 8\n\nSet 1: {9, 1, 8, 2, 5}\nSet 2: {1, 5, 2, 9, 8}\nDifference: {}\n\n\nTesting\n\nYou can compile and test your function using the following commands:\n\n\nmake                                     # compiles the program\n./testListSetDifference                  # tests with manual input, outputs to terminal\n./testListSetDifference < input-file     # tests with input from a file, outputs to terminal\n./testListSetDifference < tests/01.in    # for example, tests with input from tests/01.in\n                                           # (then manually compare with tests/01.exp)\n\n\nAfter you have manually tested your solution, you can autotest it by running ./autotest. This will run some basic tests on your program, as well as check for memory leaks/errors.\n\nIt is possible to devise your own tests by creating your own input files. See the existing input files for examples. Note that you will need to check the output yourself.",
    "starter": "struct list *listSetDifference(struct list *l1, struct list *l2) {\n    // TODO\n}",
    "answer": "static bool listContains(struct list *l, int value);\nstatic void listPrepend(struct list *l, int value);\nstatic struct node *newNode(int val);\n\nstruct list *listSetDifference(struct list *l1, struct list *l2) {\n\tstruct list *l3 = listNew();\n\t\n\tstruct node *curr = l1->head;\n\twhile (curr != NULL) {\n\t\tif (!listContains(l2, curr->value)) {\n\t\t\tlistPrepend(l3, curr->value);\n\t\t}\n\t\tcurr = curr->next;\n\t}\n\t\n\treturn l3;\n}\n\nstatic bool listContains(struct list *l, int value) {\n\tfor (struct node *curr = l->head; curr != NULL; curr = curr->next) {\n\t\tif (curr->value == value) {\n\t\t\treturn true;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false;\n}\n\nstatic void listPrepend(struct list *l, int value) {\n\tstruct node *n = newNode(value);\n\tn->next = l->head;\n\tl->head = n;\n}\n\nstatic struct node *newNode(int val) {\n\tstruct node *n = malloc(sizeof(*n));\n\tif (n == NULL) {\n\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"error: out of memory\\n\");\n\t\texit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n\t}\n\tn->value = val;\n\tn->next = NULL;\n\treturn n;\n}",
